<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40514" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-calcĭtro</span></b> ,
			āre, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to kick back</i> (of horses);
			transf. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> (<b>Poet.</b>) <i>To deny access</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Hor.
				S. 2, 1, 20</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> (Late Lat.) <i>To be petulant</i>, <i>disobedient</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incrassatus est dilectus, et recalcitravit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Deut. 32, 15</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">majestati Augustae recalcitrans,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 7, 14</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">15, 7, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">22, 11, 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
